   on the main thread? Better: worker computes h = poly(slice) which is
   (...((m0*r + m1)*r + ...)*r) so h = sum m_j * r^{n-1-j}
   To place slice starting at global block offset S with total blocks T:
   contribution = h_local * r^{T - S - n_local} = h_local * r^{blocks_after}
   We precompute r^{blocks_after} ... actually different per slice.
   Main thread multiplies each h by r^{after}.
